@startuml
actor "New Company Owner" as Owner
participant "Public Website (Registration)" as WEB
participant "Backend (Tenant Module)" as BE
database "MongoDB" as DB
actor "Superadmin" as SAdmin

== Company Self-Registration ==

Owner -> WEB : Fill Registration Form (Company Name, Slug, Admin Email, Password)
activate WEB

WEB -> BE : POST /api/v1/public/register-tenant
activate BE

BE -> BE : Validate Domain Slug & Email Uniqueness
BE -> DB : Create New Tenant (Status: 'Pending/Active')
activate DB
DB --> BE : TenantID
deactivate DB

BE -> DB : Create User Record {role: 'admin', tenantID, isOwner: true}
activate DB
DB --> BE : Success
deactivate DB

BE --> WEB : 201 Created (Redirect to Setup Wizard)
deactivate BE

WEB --> Owner : Welcome! Please complete your Org Setup
deactivate WEB

== Internal Company Setup (By Company Admin) ==

Owner -> BE : POST /api/v1/org/setup (Depts, Designations, Shifts)
BE -> DB : Save Tenant-Specific Configurations
BE --> Owner : Setup Complete. You can now onboard employees.

== Superadmin Governance ==

SAdmin -> BE : GET /api/v1/super/tenants (List all companies)
BE -> DB : Fetch Tenants
BE --> SAdmin : Tenant List
@enduml
